  ('tikal-guatemala', '10S', 'Tikal / Flores', 'Guatemala', 'Temple IV at sunrise, Peten jungle', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Guatemala', '{"expedition","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["UNESCO World Heritage Site (1979); 576 km² biosphere with 3,000+ identified Maya structures.","Temple IV rises 64.6 m (212 ft) — the tallest pre-Columbian structure in the Americas; the classic sunrise perch above the canopy.","Tikal park entry Q150 (~US$19.50) foreigners; open 06:00–18:00; sunrise/sunset permits +Q100 each (mandatory guide).","Flores/Santa Elena (FRS) Mundo Maya airport takes 4–5 daily flights from Guatemala City (GUA) on TAG Airlines & Avianca; Tikal is 65 km / ~1 hr from Flores.","Base is the island town of Flores on Lake Petén Itzá; the wildlife includes jaguars, 5 cat species, howler/spider monkeys, coatis, ocellated turkeys and 400+ birds."],"safety":{"emergency":{"police":"110","fire_ambulance":"122 / 123","tourist_assistance_PROATUR":"1500"},"hospital":"Nearest hospital in Santa Elena/Flores (~1 hr); serious cases air-evac to Guatemala City. HARD remote-medevac flag — Tikal is jungle-remote.","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"stay_in_zone":true,"malaria":"Petén is a CDC-named P. vivax malaria chemoprophylaxis department AND an annual dengue department — pre-trip travel-medicine consult + bite prevention required","water":"Bottled/filtered only","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guatemala","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:53Z","page_updated":"2026-08-13T14:45:16+01:00","source_country":"guatemala","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"Within 5km of the Mexican border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The towns of Santa Ana Huista, San Anto