ty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"2026-11-01","peak":"2026-12 to 2027-04","shoulder":"2026-05 to 2026-10 (hot/humid; hurricane exposure Aug-Oct)","fire_date":"2026-10-22","trigger_rule":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks; attaches to Mérida-base lead time","booking_lead_days":{"day_tour":"2-7","merida_base_high_season":"28-84"},"event_peaks":["Hanal Pixán / Day of the Dead 2026-10-31 to 2026-11-02","summer solstice El Adivino alignment","evening light-and-sound show (dry-cool nights)"],"selling_point":"markedly less crowded than Chichén Itzá","note":"sharpen on live tracking — Mérida occupancy curves + INAH visitor counts"},"jewels":[{"name":"Pyramid of the Magician (El Adivino)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/uxmal | Accessed