the harbour, plus the island''s rum and craft scene","si":"culinary","blurb":"keshi yena, fresh fish and Blue Curaçao at the floating market and the harbour, plus the island''s rum and craft scene","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"venue/bundle","wells":["activities","eat","shop"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culinary","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","diveglobal":"destination","entertainment":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["venue","bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Curacao?","a":"Dive discipline, not danger. Hold the no-fly 18-24h window and manage deep profiles (the Superior Producer sits at 30m). Reassuringly, Curacao Medical Center has an on-island recompression chamber - the ABC''s regional dive-emergency facility.","source":"curacao.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Curacao a liveaboard destination?","a":"No - like its ABC neighbours it is shore + day-boat diving only (packages, private charters, PADI 5-star operators), not a liveaboard base. Book it as a resort-and-boat dive trip, not a Dive Liveaboards sailing.","source":"divecuracao.info","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit and dive Curacao?","a":"Year-round - Curacao is south of the hurricane belt with warm, clear water all year. December-April is the drier peak; May-November is warmer and quieter (best value), with the odd short shower.","source":"scubatravel.co.uk","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Which Curacao dive sites should I not miss?","a":"The Tugboat (5m, beginner-perfect), the Mushroom Forest + Blue Room boat run, the Superior Producer deep wreck (30m), and a Klein Curacao islet day; many west-end sites are also shore-accessible.","source":"divecuracao.info","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is there more to Curacao than diving?","a":"Yes - it''s the ABC''s 